matter-wake-replay 1
# The sandbox at its default size. It uses every tool: it selects each
# slot, places every material, digs through a ledge and the floor, digs
# away what it placed, presses both buttons at once, selects a slot that
# does not exist and brushes outside the world. Then everything settles.
seed 1
size 480 270
brush 4
slots sand water stone
materials 6e7eb28e6efa51f0
ticks 600

# Wait while the sand and the water fall.
0 240 20 - 0
# Select stone and place two disks of it in the air, 49 cells each.
20 240 40 - 3
21 240 40 P 0
22 260 40 - 0
23 260 40 P 0
24 260 40 - 0
# Select water and pour it for ten ticks; it falls to the floor.
40 200 120 - 2
41 200 120 P 0
51 200 120 - 0
# Select sand and pour it onto the water on the right ledge.
60 360 150 - 1
61 360 150 P 0
71 360 150 - 0
# Dig a hole through the left ledge under the heap of sand.
90 120 150 D 0
96 128 150 D 0
102 136 150 D 0
108 136 150 - 0
# Dig into the floor.
150 240 268 D 0
151 240 268 - 0
# Dig away the two stone disks, 49 cells each.
180 240 40 D 0
181 240 40 - 0
182 260 40 D 0
183 260 40 - 0
# Both buttons at once: digging wins.
200 300 255 PD 0
201 300 255 - 0
# Slot 9 does not exist, so sand stays selected.
210 40 120 - 9
211 40 120 P 0
212 40 120 - 0
# The brush outside the world changes nothing.
230 -20 -20 D 0
231 500 100 P 0
232 500 100 - 0
# Then everything settles until tick 600.
